<title>SWEDEN: Nokia sees '97 market at 90-100 mln mobile phones.</title>
<headline>Nokia sees '97 market at 90-100 mln mobile phones.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecoms group Nokia said on Wednesday it expected the global mobile telephone market to total 90-100 million mobile phones this year.  </p>
<p>&quot;Last year sales reached 65 million mobile phones and in 1997 we expect a figure of 90-100 million,&quot; Nokia chief executive Jorma Ollila told a news seminar.</p>
<p>Nokia expects the number of mobile phone subscribers to increase to about 200 million this year, he said.</p>
<p>The number of subscribers currently amounts to 165 million compared to about 135 million at the beginning of the year, Ollila said.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
